WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.070
Take one kilogram of water
and one kilogram of iron.

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.410
Give each one exactly the same
amount of energy from the same

3
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:08.290
heater.

4
00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.390
Then measure their temperatures.

5
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.590
The iron has warmed up
far more than the water.

6
00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:14.750
Same mass.

7
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:15.950
Same energy.

8
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.870
So why such a different
rise in temperature?

9
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.190
In this mission, you'll meet
specific heat capacity,

10
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:25.190
a property that differs from
one material to another.

11
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.850
You'll use the equation
that links energy, mass,

12
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.870
specific heat capacity
and temperature change,

13
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:35.030
and calculate how much energy
it takes to warm something up.

14
00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:39.460
Your mission: find out why the
iron warms up so much more.
